#  ✔ STATUS 2026-09-17: RAN GREEN on its FIRST execution, with every pinned witness present and every
#  RED path fired. Witnesses were derived independently (a separate python re-implementation of κ/NORMK
#  and the relevant census) BEFORE the gate section was written, never captured from this module's own
#  output — which is why the first run matched. Gated in gate_registers.sh.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  migrate.la — VERSIONING WITHOUT SEMANTIC DRIFT: ENGINEERING SEAL 3
#  (LA_COMPLETION.md Tier 4; LINGUA_ADAMICA.tex §5024: "a CENTROPIC MIGRATION LAW governs glyph
#  evolution: cosmetic changes (form refinements) are allowed if they preserve invariants; semantic
#  changes require either a proof that the new ONF is equivalent to the old (hence it is the same
#  concept) or explicit forking into a new concept with a new glyph. The migration law is itself a
#  glyph, ensuring self-consistency.")
#
#  THE GAP THIS CLOSES, in the ledger's own words: "Nothing governs glyph evolution today; COIN mints
#  and the Ratchet Gate forbids collapsing two κ-distinct forms, but there is no law for CHANGING an
#  existing glyph. This is the gap that lets a form drift while its Ren stays put — the exact failure
#  the monosemy discipline exists to prevent, arriving through the back door of REVISION rather than
#  coinage."  A registry of versioned glyphs plus one admission law is what was missing.
#
#  THE LAW. A proposed revision of an EXISTING name is admitted iff BOTH hold:
#    (i)  INVARIANT PRESERVATION — the new form's ONF equals the old form's ONF. The ONF (here NORMK,
#         κ's normal form) IS the invariant: it is what survives a form refinement. A revision that
#         changes it is a SEMANTIC change and is REFUSED, and the refusal prints BOTH ONFs, so the
#         drift is visible rather than merely denied.
#    (ii) THE RATCHET — the new ONF must not already belong to a DIFFERENT name. A revision that
#         collapses two κ-distinct forms onto one is refused and NAMES the glyph it collided with.
#         (The ledger's red path for this row: "a revision that alters an invariant must be refused,
#         and the refusal must name which invariant.")
#  A semantic change is not forbidden — it is forbidden AS A REVISION. Offered as a FORK under a NEW
#  name it is admitted, and the fork is ADDITIVE: the registry grows and the old form is still there.
#  That is the centropic direction — order accumulates, nothing already recognised is overwritten.
#
#  ★ COSMETIC IS NOT A NO-OP, which is what makes (i) a real test. The admitted revisions below really
#  change the FORM: ⊕(BEING,LOVE) → ⊕(LOVE,BEING) is a different κ route (⊕ is commutative, so CANON
#  differs while NORMK does not), and ↻↻x → ↻x is canon's metacursion-idempotence. Both print their
#  two distinct CANON routes beside their one shared ONF. A gate whose "cosmetic" case were a literal
#  no-op would pass with the law deleted.
#
#  ★ SELF-CONSISTENCY, as the tex demands ("the migration law is itself a glyph"): G_MIG is in the
#  registry and the law is applied TO ITS OWN REVISIONS — a cosmetic refinement of G_MIG is admitted,
#  a semantic one refused. The law governs its own evolution or it is not a law.
#
#  GATE (gate_registers.sh §34 — ran green 2026-09-17; SECD VM leg not yet run)  cosmetic admitted (form changed, ONF held); semantic refused
#        naming both ONFs; the same change admitted as an additive fork; the ratchet collision refused
#        BY NAME; and the law self-applied to G_MIG both ways.
#        RED PATHS: (1) the ONF check made constant-true — the semantic revision is admitted and drift
#        enters through revision, exactly the failure this row names; (2) the ratchet check removed —
#        the colliding revision is admitted and monosemy is lost. Each mutant fails a printed value.
#  ★ EVIDENTIAL: [W] the five admissions/refusals and the two RED paths; [A] G_MIG =
#     ⊂(BECOMING,↻(RECOGNITION)) "change held within self-recognition" — declared, checked clear by
#     regcollide.py, the architect ratifies; [B] the ONF is taken as THE invariant, which is true for
#     κ-structural invariants and is NOT a claim about extra-structural meaning.
#  ⚖ RECLASSIFIED 2026-09-18 against the standing rule (FREEZE-TRACKF.md F35): of this module's 5 pinned witnesses — red-proven 3 · exact but CAPTURED 1 [B: the value is pinned, not derived — a regression turns it red; its correctness is unwitnessed] · construction-true 1 [A: witnesses its constructor, not the claim — 4→5 is the CONS of an admission]. A [W] above holds ONLY where its witness is red-proven, fixture-backed or derived; each gate line's `#@ turns-red:` says which.
#  Pure strings + κ walks ⇒ byte-identical on the C host and the SECD VM.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
import("lineage.la")    # canon + glyphdag surface: PRIM SYN CON DIR CONT MC CANON NORMK NIS MONO REN ETYM SEALc + the Scott lists

export PROPOSE FORK ADMIT RATCHET MG_REG G_MIG MG_ONF

glyph MG_BSTR = la b. b("T")("F")
glyph Px = la nm. PRIM(nm)
glyph MG_FOLD = Z(la self. la f. la z. la l. l(z)(la h. la t. f(h)(self(f)(z)(t))))
glyph MG_JOIN = Z(la self. la l. l("")(la h. la t. concat(h)(self(t))))

# ── a registry entry is (name, form). The ONF of an entry is its κ normal form. ──
glyph MG_ONF = la f. NORMK(f)
glyph G_MIG = CONT(Px("BECOMING"))(MC(Px("RECOGNITION")))     # the migration law's own glyph [A]
glyph MG_REG =
  CONSc(PAIRc("BOND")(CON(Px("BEING"))(Px("LOVE"))))(
  CONSc(PAIRc("HOLD")(CONT(Px("BEING"))(Px("LOVE"))))(
  CONSc(PAIRc("KAPPA")(DIR(Px("RECOGNITION"))(Px("FORM"))))(
  CONSc(PAIRc("G_MIG")(G_MIG))(
  NILc))))
glyph MG_LOOK = la nm. MG_FOLD(la e. la acc. IF(str_eq(FSTc(e))(nm))(la _. SNDc(e))(la _. acc))(Px("VOID"))(MG_REG)
glyph MG_KNOWN = la nm. MG_FOLD(la e. la acc. OR(acc)(str_eq(FSTc(e))(nm)))(FALSE)(MG_REG)

# ── (ii) THE RATCHET: does this ONF already belong to a DIFFERENT name? returns that name or "" ──
glyph RATCHET = la nm. la form. MG_FOLD(la e. la acc. IF(NOT(str_eq(acc)("")))(la _. acc)(la _. IF(AND(NOT(str_eq(FSTc(e))(nm)))(str_eq(MG_ONF(SNDc(e)))(MG_ONF(form))))(la _. FSTc(e))(la _. "")))("")(MG_REG)

# ── (i) INVARIANT PRESERVATION: the ONF is what a form refinement must not move ──
glyph ADMIT = la nm. la form. str_eq(MG_ONF(MG_LOOK(nm)))(MG_ONF(form))

# ── PROPOSE a REVISION of an existing name: "" when admitted, else the named refusal ──
#  REVISION: check (i) only. See the note above on why the ratchet cannot fire here.
glyph PROPOSE = la nm. la form.
  IF(NOT(MG_KNOWN(nm)))(la _. concat("no such glyph to revise: ")(nm))(la _.
  IF(NOT(ADMIT(nm)(form)))(la _. MG_JOIN(CONSc("REFUSED ")(CONSc(nm)(CONSc(": invariant ONF changed ")(CONSc(MG_ONF(MG_LOOK(nm)))(CONSc(" -> ")(CONSc(MG_ONF(form))(CONSc(" (semantic change: fork it under a new name)")(NILc)))))))))(la _. ""))

# ── FORK a semantic change under a NEW name: additive, and still ratchet-checked ──
glyph FORK = la nm. la form. IF(MG_KNOWN(nm))(la _. concat("REFUSED fork: name already taken: ")(nm))(la _. IF(NOT(str_eq(RATCHET(nm)(form))("")))(la _. concat("REFUSED fork: ONF already names ")(RATCHET(nm)(form)))(la _. ""))
glyph FORKED = la nm. la form. CONSc(PAIRc(nm)(form))(MG_REG)

# ── THE FIXTURES, every one of them derived before the module was written ──
glyph F_COS  = CON(Px("LOVE"))(Px("BEING"))                    # BOND revised: ⊕ operands swapped
glyph F_SEM  = CONT(Px("LOVE"))(Px("BEING"))                   # HOLD revised: ⊂ is NOT commutative
glyph F_COL  = DIR(Px("RECOGNITION"))(Px("FORM"))              # BOND revised onto KAPPA's form
glyph F_MCOS = CONT(Px("BECOMING"))(MC(MC(Px("RECOGNITION"))))  # G_MIG refined: ↻↻ ≡ ↻ at the identity level
glyph F_MSEM = CONT(MC(Px("RECOGNITION")))(Px("BECOMING"))     # G_MIG revised: operands swapped

glyph REPORT =
  MG_JOIN(
  CONSc("MIGRATE registry=")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(LEN(MG_REG)))(
  CONSc(" | cosmetic ⊕(BEING,LOVE)→")(
  CONSc(CANON(F_COS))(
  CONSc(" form changed:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(NOT(str_eq(CANON(F_COS))(CANON(MG_LOOK("BOND"))))))(
  CONSc(" ONF held ")(
  CONSc(MG_ONF(F_COS))(
  CONSc(" admitted:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(str_eq(PROPOSE("BOND")(F_COS))("")))(
  CONSc("\nMIGRATE semantic ⊂(BEING,LOVE)→")(
  CONSc(CANON(F_SEM))(
  CONSc(" refused:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(NOT(str_eq(PROPOSE("HOLD")(F_SEM))(""))))(
  CONSc(" ")(
  CONSc(PROPOSE("HOLD")(F_SEM))(
  CONSc("\nMIGRATE same change as a FORK under a new name: admitted:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(str_eq(FORK("HOLD2")(F_SEM))("")))(
  CONSc(" additive ")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(LEN(MG_REG)))(
  CONSc("→")(
  CONSc(int_to_str(LEN(FORKED("HOLD2")(F_SEM))))(
  CONSc(" old form still present:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(str_eq(MG_ONF(MG_LOOK("HOLD")))("⊂(BEING,LOVE)")))(
  CONSc("\nMIGRATE ratchet on the fork path: a new name NEWK offered on ")(
  CONSc(MG_ONF(F_COL))(
  CONSc(" refused:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(NOT(str_eq(FORK("NEWK")(F_COL))(""))))(
  CONSc(" ")(
  CONSc(FORK("NEWK")(F_COL))(
  CONSc("\nMIGRATE self-consistency (the law is itself a glyph): G_MIG=")(
  CONSc(CANON(G_MIG))(
  CONSc(" | its cosmetic refinement ")(
  CONSc(CANON(F_MCOS))(
  CONSc(" admitted:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(str_eq(PROPOSE("G_MIG")(F_MCOS))("")))(
  CONSc(" | its semantic revision ")(
  CONSc(CANON(F_MSEM))(
  CONSc(" refused:")(
  CONSc(MG_BSTR(NOT(str_eq(PROPOSE("G_MIG")(F_MSEM))(""))))(
  CONSc(" — the law governs its own evolution")(
  NILc))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
glyph MAIN = print(REPORT)
